Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 09:22:15 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 125/154] fix(quit): the hold-to-quit HUD follows the overlay
 theme and keeps its keycaps
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The HUD has no WebContents, so the overlay theme never reached it and
it always mixed the brand crimson. The brand book themes now live in
C++ too (atrium_overlay_themes.cc, pinned to the book by the node
test), the window writes the chosen palette to local state whenever
the theme is applied, and the HUD reads it back. In the native look
the Cmd and Q caps kept no chip at all and read as plain words: they
now draw in the ink at a low alpha.

Signed-off-by: János Mikó <693558+janosmiko@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 chrome/browser/ui/BUILD.gn                               | 2 ++
 chrome/browser/ui/cocoa/BUILD.gn                         | 1 +
 chrome/browser/ui/cocoa/confirm_quit.cc                  | 3 +++
 chrome/browser/ui/cocoa/confirm_quit_panel_controller.mm | 6 ++++--
 chrome/common/pref_names.h                               | 8 +++++++-
 5 files changed, 17 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/ui/BUILD.gn b/chrome/browser/ui/BUILD.gn
index 162d48e7b9ae5..8146fd31c0881 100644
